      "description": "Watch Serbia vs Greece highlights and goals from UEFA Nations League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 24, 2026. A tense tactical encounter On September 24, 2026, the UEFA Nations League featured an electrifying clash between Serbia and Greece , a match defined by tactical grit and shifting momentum. In front of 5,701 fans, both teams displayed high intensity, turning the pitch into a theater of determination throughout the 90 minutes. Serbia strikes early Serbia wasted no time establishing their presence. Just 4 minutes in, Andrija Zivkovic fired home a left-footed strike following a clinical assist from Dusan Tadic , giving the hosts an early advantage. The momentum appeared to be entirely with the home side shortly after, but a powerful attempt by Konstantinos Karetsas rattled the post, serving as a warning that the contest was far from settled. Greece’s stunning fightback The second half saw Greece slowly take control of the midfield battle. Their persistence bore fruit in the 74th minute when Christos Tzolis expertly tucked away a goal assisted by Vangelis Pavlidis . As the clock ticked into stoppage time, the tension reached its peak. In a dramatic conclusion at the 90+5 minute mark, Anastasios Douvikas rose to meet a brilliant delivery from Konstantinos Tsimikas , heading the ball into the net to complete a stunning turnaround and secure the win for the visitors."
